#
# Text is shaped with its script, without libharfbuzz-icu.
#
# WebKit maps each text run's ICU script to HarfBuzz's with
# hb_icu_script_to_script() from libharfbuzz-icu, which Sailfish OS does not
# install on the phone. The engine carried Atlantic's stand-in library
# (compat/libharfbuzz-icu.so.0), which returns HB_SCRIPT_UNKNOWN for every
# script: Arabic, Hebrew, Indic and Thai runs were shaped without their
# script (no joining or reordering features chosen for it), and an RTL
# locale's default writing direction came out as Default. WebKit now does
# what harfbuzz-icu does, hb_script_from_string() on the script's ISO 15924
# code (HarfBuzzICUScript.h), and no longer links libharfbuzz-icu.
#
